  "surprise": "P02 follow-up: raising decoupled Muon weight decay from 3x to 10x (MUON_WD 0.03 -> 0.1; peak per-step shrinkage 3e-4 -> 1e-3, cumulative factor ~0.07 vs ~0.46) on incumbent 069-claude scored 359/335/364 on seeds 0/1/2 versus 335/285/362: exact means 352.666667 versus 327.333333, +25.33 (+7.7%); paired +24/+50/+2. Keep under the strictly-higher three-seed rule. Inside the registered -60 to +30 range but near its top, far above the central guess of -5: I expected the trend to break, and it did not. The feared sharpness failure did not appear in pretraining: 4784/4750/4776 steps, final val loss 0.0911/0.0913/0.0961 vs 0.0923/0.0914/0.0967 (slightly lower, not the predicted rise), though held-out greedy dipped 0.987/0.987/0.9875 vs 0.9925/0.991/0.9905. Unlike 069, where gains came only late, this time RL improved from round 1: targets after round 1 were 200/324/206 vs 172/159/155 (seed 1 round-1 acc 0.129 vs 0.043), round-4 acc was 0.464/0.460/0.485 vs 0.440/0.438/0.454, and RL-solved was 788/783/838 vs 762/743/792 (+26/+40/+46, every seed). Eval gains are spread across 7-10 lines (10-line 19/22/25 vs 17/15/24; 11-line 1/1/2 vs 0/0/1). Across 1x/3x/10x decay the scores were 316/327/353, a monotone trend consistent with the plasticity mechanism (smaller Muon weights let the frozen RL AdamW move them further). Weight norms were not logged, so that mechanism is still unverified. Cost: totals 1048/971/1079 s vs 941-993, shrinking headroom under the 1200 s cap. Next: MUON_WD 0.3 (30x) to find the break point, ideally also logging per-matrix spectral norms.",
